  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnerships for Growth: Women Entrepreneurs Finance (We-Fi) Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Women Entrepreneurs Finance Initiative (We-Fi) is a collaborative partnership between governments, Multilateral Development Banks, and private sector stakeholders looking to address the financing gap facing women by providing access to finance, financial services, capacity building, networking opportunities, and opportunities to connect with global and domestic markets. We-Fi&#x2019;s Women Entrepreneurs Finance Code is a commitment by financial institutions to work together to increase funding provided to women-led SMEs. This partnership forms part of the Jobs and Inclusive Growth Centre of Expertise (CoE) which will also leverage the knowledge and expert advice of the initiative to inform other components of the COE.</narrative>
  </description>
